# 🛡️ Fraud Detection Enterprise Backend (`fraud_detection` v1.0.0)

[![Python 3.10+](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.10%2B-blue.svg)](https://www.python.org/)
[![Code Coverage](https://img.shields.io/badge/coverage-93%25-brightgreen.svg)](tests/)
[![Code Style: Ruff](https://img.shields.io/badge/code%20style-ruff-000000.svg)](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff)

An enterprise-grade, framework-agnostic Python backend package for real-time and batch financial transaction fraud inference, probability calibration, risk thresholding, and business explainability.

---

## 🏗️ Architecture & Pipeline Flow

```text
Client Application / Future API Layer
                 │
                 ▼
          PredictionEngine (Facade)
                 │
                 ▼
         PredictionService (Orchestrator)
                 │
 ┌───────────────┼───────────────┬───────────────┬───────────────┬───────────────┐
 │               │               │               │               │               │
 ▼               ▼               ▼               ▼               ▼               ▼
Feature      Production       CatBoost        Isotonic        Threshold       Explainability
Validator    Preprocessor     Champion        Calibrator       Engine          Engine
(Schema Check) (Impute/Scale) (Raw Score)    (Posterior Prob) (Risk Tiers)    (SHAP Drivers)
 │               │               │               │               │               │
 └───────────────┴───────────────┼───────────────┴───────────────┴───────────────┘
                                 ▼
                         PredictionBuilder
                                 │
                                 ▼
                         PredictionSession (Typed Response)
```

---

## 🏛️ Model Registry & Asset Structure

```text
models/
├── registry.json                    # Active production model pointer
└── champion/
    ├── model_v1.joblib              # Tuned CatBoost Classifier binary
    ├── preprocessing_v1.joblib      # Scikit-Learn ColumnTransformer pipeline
    ├── calibrator_v1.joblib         # Isotonic CalibratedClassifierCV binary
    ├── threshold_v1.json            # Business-cost optimized decision threshold (0.26)
    ├── metadata_v1.json             # Model version & evaluation registry metadata
    ├── feature_schema_v1.json       # Expected 78 raw input features schema
    └── feature_order_v1.json        # Expected 61 processed feature vector order
```

---

## ⚡ Inference Performance Benchmarks

*Note: On the local development environment, batch inference over 1,000 transactions completed in approximately 36 ms, illustrating the efficiency of vectorized inference.*

| Batch Size | Total Latency (ms) | Per-Transaction Latency (ms) | Mode / Explanations |
| :---: | :---: | :---: | :--- |
| **1** | `159.00 ms` | `159.00 ms` | Real-time + Full SHAP Investigator Card |
| **10** | `31.68 ms` | `3.17 ms` | Vectorized Batch + SHAP Explanations |
| **100** | `41.54 ms` | `0.42 ms` | Vectorized Batch + SHAP Explanations |
| **1,000** | `36.55 ms` | `0.04 ms` | Fast Vectorized Batch (Explanations Bypassed) |

---

## 🚀 Quickstart & Usage

```python
from fraud_detection import EngineFactory, PredictionEngine

# 1. Initialize engine using explicit dependency factory
engine: PredictionEngine = EngineFactory.create()

# 2. Real-time Single Transaction Inference
transaction = {
    "Amount_Paid": 500.0,
    "Amount_Received": 500.0,
    "is_amount_outlier": 0.0,
    # ... remaining raw transaction fields
}

response = engine.predict(transaction)
print(f"Request ID: {response.request_id}")
print(f"Decision: {response.decision}")             # e.g. APPROVED_WITH_MONITORING
print(f"Risk Level: {response.risk_level}")           # e.g. RiskLevel.MEDIUM
print(f"Calibrated Prob: {response.calibrated_probability:.4f}")
print(f"Top Risk Driver: {response.top_risk_drivers[0]['feature']}")

# 3. Vectorized Batch Inference
sessions = engine.predict_batch(batch_df, include_explanations=False)
print(f"Processed {len(sessions)} batch predictions.")
```

